\ Fail-closed rank checks for the year-candidate ledger.
\ The candidate record and status must not change when a rank is
\ invalid. The list reader also must not dereference NIL when
\ its count is accidentally larger than its real linked-list length.
\ These are fast synthetic checks: no sauce calculation is needed.
\ CAL compilation and native execution remain outstanding.

To check invalid year candidate ranks:
  Make synthetic year gates.
  Gather eligible year candidates.
  If the eligible year count is not 11,
    put "The synthetic year rank setup has the wrong number of years." into the check report; exit.
  Put 1 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the selected year available is not 1,
    put "The first valid year rank was rejected." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -3,
    put "The first year rank selected an incorrect opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put 0 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the selected year available is not 0,
    put "Year candidate rank zero was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -3,
    put "Invalid rank zero overwrote the prior chosen year." into the check report; exit.
  Put 12 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the selected year available is not 0,
    put "A rank above the eligible count was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -3,
    put "An out-of-range rank changed the chosen year." into the check report; exit.
  Put 11 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the selected year available is not 1,
    put "The final valid year rank was rejected after invalid ranks." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -2,
    put "The final valid year rank selected the wrong opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put 100 into the eligible year count.
  Put 99 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the selected year available is not 0,
    put "A truncated year ledger accepted a missing linked record." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -2,
    put "A truncated ledger overwrote the last valid chosen year." into the check report; exit.
  Destroy the eligible year ledger.
  Destroy the nearby gate ledger.

\ This test uses the same candidate and checks the ordinal behavior
\ when calculation day falls exactly on the opening or closing gate.
The boundarytestday is a calendar day.

To check synthetic year boundary containment:
  Put -15055671 into the year selection day.
  Make synthetic year gates.
  Gather eligible year candidates.
  Put 1 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the selected year available is not 1,
    put "The boundary test did not select a synthetic year." into the check report; exit.
  Put the chosen year's opening day into the boundarytestday.
  Evaluate native year containment given the chosen year and the boundarytestday.
  If the native year containment result is 1,
    put "A year incorrectly contains its own opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  Put the chosen year's closing day into the boundarytestday.
  Evaluate native year containment given the chosen year and the boundarytestday.
  If the native year containment result is not 1,
    put "A year incorrectly excludes its own closing gate." into the check report; exit.
  Destroy the eligible year ledger.
  Destroy the nearby gate ledger.
